{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/39157-bargains-to-clear-the-fog-of-ages","id":39157,"title":"Bargains to clear the Fog of Ages...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-29T22:34:55-08:00","id":39157,"title":"Bargains to clear the Fog of Ages...","content":"So, I've got a vampire who has experienced a long torpor. He's haunted by memories of something important to him he's lost ; some cause, some ideal, some personal totem that was so very vital to him that he struggled to preserve it through his long sleep... but failed. Now, after a lifetime of drifting slowly farther away from a truth increasingly obscured by time, he feels a haunting sense of loss he can't quite identity.<br /> <br /> The OOC details? More or less, the vampire had a beef with another vampire that was very important to him at the time. If he actually knew the truth? He might be underwhelmed. It's the 'shadow' of the event that has impacted the creature so severely - the assumption that the truth he has lost has some sort of greater, almost mystical, significance.<br /> <br /> In any case, an Unchained is sitting down to bargain with this creature. The question I have is - to what degree (if any) would an Unchained be able to offer a remedy to the Fog of Ages? The Unchained has literally read through the vampire's extensive journals, so is fully aware of the existential angst the creature is experiencing and how vulnerable it is to being offered a 'salve'. Is such a salve possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:01:44-08:00","id":39172,"title":"","content":"I don't think an Unchained could just 'magic' such a salve via pact, but a demon could probably provide that salve via its investigative Embeds, Exploits, Form Abilities, Interlocks, Merits, etc.\u2014depending on the nature of the truth in question. Demons are quite good at gathering information, if I understand correctly.<br /> <br /> Of course, even if a salve of truth proved impossible, an Unchained with the right combination of powers could create a salve of lies, false memories, and fake evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:29:00-08:00","id":39475,"title":"","content":"The fog of ages is kinda removed in Blood and Smoke. It happens occasionally still, along with waking up as someone else. If your dead set on having the fog be a major thing (Its kind of an odd inconvenience that sometimes occurs now) then removing it completely is going to be some major wonkery, and would generally fall into the 6+ power region (at least in mage it would likely be 7 dots).<br /> <br /> If just trying to restore memory that is currently lost, I wouldn't see that as too terribly difficult and likely possible however. If removing the fog as a threat... no, if restoring memories... I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> As far as a pact goes... I'm still not comfortable in what all a pact can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T16:34:31-08:00","id":39683,"title":"","content":"Pacts can't do much.<br /> The are inherently weaker than Changeling Pledges (to use a familiar mechanic).<br /> Except they can remove reationships (and pretty much only remove reationships), as if they never happened,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}